{"id":"mahabharata-5-145","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":145,"title":"पञ्चचत्वारिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 145 · Krishna reports to the Pandavas: Bhishma's words","summary":{"en":"Back at Upaplavya, Krishna tells the Pandavas what happened in Hastinapura, beginning with Bhishma's speech in the assembly. Bhishma recalled how he had renounced the throne and preserved the Kuru line, and urged Duryodhana to heed his elders and not destroy the family.","kn":"ಉಪಪ್ಲವ್ಯಕ್ಕೆ ಮರಳಿದ ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ಸಭೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಭೀಷ್ಮನ ಭಾಷಣದಿಂದ ಆರಂಭಿಸಿ ಹಸ್ತಿನಾಪುರದಲ್ಲಿ ನಡೆದದ್ದನ್ನು ಪಾಂಡವರಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತಾನು ಸಿಂಹಾಸನ ತ್ಯಜಿಸಿ ಕುರುವಂಶವನ್ನು ಉಳಿಸಿದ್ದನ್ನು ನೆನೆದು, ಹಿರಿಯರ ಮಾತು ಕೇಳು, ಕುಲ ನಾಶಮಾಡಬೇಡ ಎಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮನು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನನ್ನು ಒತ್ತಾಯಿಸಿದನು.","hi":"उपप्लव्य लौटकर श्रीकृष्ण पाण्डवों को हस्तिनापुर की घटनाएँ बताते हैं, सभा में भीष्म के भाषण से आरम्भ करके। भीष्म ने याद दिलाया था कि उन्होंने कैसे सिंहासन त्यागकर कुरुवंश की रक्षा की, और दुर्योधन से बड़ों की बात मानने और कुल का नाश न करने का आग्रह किया था।","te":"ఉపప్లావ్యానికి తిరిగివచ్చిన శ్రీకృష్ణుడు సభలో భీష్ముని ప్రసంగంతో మొదలుపెట్టి హస్తినాపురంలో జరిగినది పాండవులకు చెబుతాడు. తాను సింహాసనాన్ని త్యజించి కురువంశాన్ని కాపాడిన తీరును గుర్తుచేసి, పెద్దల మాట వినమని, కులాన్ని నాశనం చేయవద్దని భీష్ముడు దుర్యోధనుని కోరాడు.","ta":"உபப்லவ்யத்துக்குத் திரும்பிய ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் சபையில் பீஷ்மரின் உரையிலிருந்து தொடங்கி ஹஸ்தினாபுரத்தில் நடந்ததைப் பாண்டவர்களிடம் சொல்கிறார். தாம் அரியணையைத் துறந்து குரு குலத்தைக் காத்ததை நினைவுகூர்ந்து, மூத்தோர் சொல் கேள், குலத்தை அழிக்காதே என்று பீஷ்மர் துரியோதனனை வற்புறுத்தினார்.","ml":"ഉപപ്ലവ്യത്തിൽ തിരിച്ചെത്തിയ കൃഷ്ണൻ ഹസ്തിനപുരത്ത് നടന്നതെല്ലാം പാണ്ഡവരോട് പറയുന്നു; സഭയിലെ ഭീഷ്മരുടെ പ്രസംഗത്തിൽനിന്ന് തുടങ്ങുന്നു. സിംഹാസനം ഉപേക്ഷിച്ച് കുരുവംശം സംരക്ഷിച്ചതും, മുതിർന്നവരെ അനുസരിച്ച് കുടുംബത്തെ നശിപ്പിക്കരുതെന്ന് ദുര്യോധനനെ ഉപദേശിച്ചതും ഭീഷ്മർ ഓർമ്മിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.145; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"कर्णोपनिवादपर्व","titleEn":"Karnopanivada Parva (The secret talks with Karna)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"आगम्य हास्तिनपुरादुपप्लव्यमरिंदमः ।\nपाण्डवानां यथावृत्तं केशवः सर्वमुक्तवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Returning from Hastinapura to Upaplavya, Keshava, tamer of foes, told the Pandavas everything that had happened."}},{"n":2,"text":"संभाष्य सुचिरं कालं मन्त्रयित्वा पुनः पुनः ।\nस्वमेवावसथं शौरिर्विश्रामार्थं जगाम ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"After talking for a long time and consulting again and again, Shauri went to his own lodging to rest."}},{"n":3,"text":"विसृज्य सर्वान्नृपतीन्विराटप्रमुखांस्तदा ।\nपाण्डवा भ्रातरः पञ्च भानावस्तंगते सति ॥","meaning":{"en":"After dismissing all the kings, headed by Virata, the five Pandava brothers, when the sun had set,"}},{"n":4,"text":"संध्यामुपास्य ध्यायन्तस्तमेव गतमानसाः ।\nआनाय्य कृष्णं दाशार्हं पुनर्मन्त्रममन्त्रयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"performed the twilight rite, and with their minds fixed on him alone, brought Krishna, the Dasharha, back and took counsel again."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"त्वया नागपुरं गत्वा सभायां धृतराष्ट्रजः ।\nकिमुक्तः पुण्डरीकाक्ष तन्नः शंसितुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lotus-eyed one, you went to Nagapura; tell us what you said to Dhritarashtra's son in the assembly."}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"मया नागपुरं गत्वा सभायां धृतराष्ट्रजः ।\nतथ्यं पथ्यं हितं चोक्तो न च गृह्णाति दुर्मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I went to Nagapura and in the assembly told Dhritarashtra's son what was true, wholesome and good, but the ill-minded one does not accept it."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"तस्मिन्नुत्पथमापन्ने कुरुवृद्धः पितामहः ।\nकिमुक्तवान्हृषीकेश दुर्योधनममर्षणम् ।\nआचार्यो वा महाबाहो भारद्वाजः किमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he had taken the wrong path, Hrishikesha, what did the Kuru elder, the grandfather, say to impatient Duryodhana? What did the teacher, Bharadvaja's son, mighty-armed one, say?"}},{"n":8,"text":"पिता यवीयानस्माकं क्षत्ता धर्मभृतां वरः ।\nपुत्रशोकाभिसंतप्तः किमाह धृतराष्ट्रजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Our younger father Vidura, the best of those who uphold dharma, burning with grief for his sons' fate, what did he say to Dhritarashtra's son?"}},{"n":9,"text":"किं च सर्वे नृपतयः सभायां ये समासते ।\nउक्तवन्तो यथातत्त्वं तद्ब्रूहि त्वं जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"And what did all the kings seated in the assembly say? Tell us, Janardana, exactly as it was."}},{"n":10,"text":"उक्तवान्हि भवान्सर्वं वचनं कुरुमुख्ययोः ।\nकामलोभाभिभूतस्य मन्दस्य प्राज्ञमानिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have told us every speech of the two Kuru chiefs, to that fool, overcome by desire and greed, who thinks himself wise."}},{"n":11,"text":"अप्रियं हृदये मह्यं तन्न तिष्ठति केशव ।\nतेषां वाक्यानि गोविन्द श्रोतुमिच्छाम्यहं विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Keshava, their unwelcome words stay in my heart; Govinda, lord, I want to hear them."}},{"n":12,"text":"यथा च नाभिपद्येत कालस्तात तथा कुरु ।\nभवान्हि नो गतिः कृष्ण भवान्नाथो भवान्गुरुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do so, my friend, that time is not wasted. You are our refuge, Krishna, you are our protector, you are our teacher."}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"शृणु राजन्यथा वाक्यमुक्तो राजा सुयोधनः ।\nमध्ये कुरूणां राजेन्द्र सभायां तन्निबोध मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, hear how King Suyodhana was addressed in the middle of the Kurus, in the assembly; listen to it from me."}},{"n":14,"text":"मया वै श्राविते वाक्ये जहास धृतराष्ट्रजः ।\nअथ भीष्मः सुसंक्रुद्ध इदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I had given my message, Dhritarashtra's son laughed. Then Bhishma, greatly angered, spoke these words."}},{"n":15,"text":"दुर्योधन निबोधेदं कुलार्थे यद्ब्रवीमि ते ।\nतच्छ्रुत्वा राजशार्दूल स्वकुलस्य हितं कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Duryodhana, listen to what I tell you for the sake of the family; having heard it, tiger among kings, do what is good for your own line."}},{"n":16,"text":"मम तात पिता राजञ्शंतनुर्लोकविश्रुतः ।\nतस्याहमेक एवासं पुत्रः पुत्रवतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"My dear son, my father, King Shantanu, was famed in the world; I was his only son, the best of men with sons."}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्य बुद्धिः समुत्पन्ना द्वितीयः स्यात्कथं सुतः ।\nएकपुत्रमपुत्रं वै प्रवदन्ति मनीषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The thought arose in him: how might there be a second son? The wise say one with a single son is childless."}},{"n":18,"text":"न चोच्छेदं कुलं यायाद्विस्तीर्येत कथं यशः ।\nतस्याहमीप्सितं बुद्ध्वा कालीं मातरमावहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He wished that the family not die out and his fame spread wide. Understanding his wish, I brought home Kali as my mother."}},{"n":19,"text":"प्रतिज्ञां दुष्करां कृत्वा पितुरर्थे कुलस्य च ।\nअराजा चोर्ध्वरेताश्च यथा सुविदितं तव ।\nप्रतीतो निवसाम्येष प्रतिज्ञामनुपालयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Making a hard vow for my father's sake and for the family, to be no king and to be one of upward-flowing seed, as you well know, I live on, trusted, keeping that vow."}},{"n":20,"text":"तस्यां जज्ञे महाबाहुः श्रीमान्कुरुकुलोद्वहः ।\nविचित्रवीर्यो धर्मात्मा कनीयान्मम पार्थिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In her was born mighty-armed, glorious Vichitravirya, upholder of the Kuru line, righteous, my younger brother and king."}},{"n":21,"text":"स्वर्यातेऽहं पितरि तं स्वराज्ये संन्यवेशयम् ।\nविचित्रवीर्यं राजानं भृत्यो भूत्वा ह्यधश्चरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When my father had gone to heaven, I set Vichitravirya in his own kingdom as king, becoming his servant, walking below him."}},{"n":22,"text":"तस्याहं सदृशान्दारान्राजेन्द्र समुदावहम् ।\nजित्वा पार्थिवसंघातमपि ते बहुशः श्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, I brought him wives who suited him, after defeating a host of kings, as you have often heard."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततो रामेण समरे द्वन्द्वयुद्धमुपागमम् ।\nस हि रामभयादेभिर्नागरैर्विप्रवासितः ।\nदारेष्वतिप्रसक्तश्च यक्ष्माणं समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I met Rama in a duel in battle. Driven out by these townspeople for fear of Rama, and too fond of his wives, he fell ill with consumption."}},{"n":24,"text":"यदा त्वराजके राष्ट्रे न ववर्ष सुरेश्वरः ।\nतदाभ्यधावन्मामेव प्रजाः क्षुद्भयपीडिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the lord of the gods did not rain on the kingdom without a king, the people, tormented by hunger and fear, ran to me.\""}},{"text":"प्रजा ऊचुः","meaning":{"en":"The people said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"उपक्षीणाः प्रजाः सर्वा राजा भव भवाय नः ।\nईतयो नुद भद्रं ते शंतनोः कुलवर्धन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"All the people are wasting away. Be king, for our welfare. Drive away the plagues. May good come to you, increaser of Shantanu's line."}},{"n":26,"text":"पीड्यन्ते ते प्रजाः सर्वा व्याधिभिर्भृशदारुणैः ।\nअल्पावशिष्टा गाङ्गेय ताः परित्रातुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"All your people are tormented by dreadful diseases, and few remain, son of Ganga. You should save them."}},{"n":27,"text":"व्याधीन्प्रणुद्य वीर त्वं प्रजा धर्मेण पालय ।\nत्वयि जीवति मा राष्ट्रं विनाशमुपगच्छतु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hero, drive away the diseases and rule the people by dharma. While you live, let the kingdom not come to ruin.\""}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":28,"text":"प्रजानां क्रोशतीनां वै नैवाक्षुभ्यत मे मनः ।\nप्रतिज्ञां रक्षमाणस्य सद्वृत्तं स्मरतस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Though my people cried out, my mind was not shaken, as I kept my vow and remembered good conduct."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततः पौरा महाराज माता काली च मे शुभा ।\nभृत्याः पुरोहिताचार्या ब्राह्मणाश्च बहुश्रुताः ।\nमामूचुर्भृशसंतप्ता भव राजेति संततम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the townsfolk, my mother Kali the fortunate, the servants, priests, teachers, and learned brahmins constantly urged me in deep distress: 'Be king."}},{"n":30,"text":"प्रतीपरक्षितं राष्ट्रं त्वां प्राप्य विनशिष्यति ।\nस त्वमस्मद्धितार्थं वै राजा भव महामते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A kingdom guarded by an enemy will perish when it comes to you. So, wise one, be king for our good.'"}},{"n":31,"text":"इत्युक्तः प्राञ्जलिर्भूत्वा दुःखितो भृशमातुरः ।\nतेभ्यो न्यवेदयं पुत्र प्रतिज्ञां पितृगौरवात् ।\nऊर्ध्वरेता ह्यराजा च कुलस्यार्थे पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, I folded my hands, deeply pained and troubled, and out of respect for my father I told them of my vow, my son: that for the family's sake I was to be childless and no king."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततोऽहं प्राञ्जलिर्भूत्वा मातरं संप्रसादयम् ।\nनाम्ब शंतनुना जातः कौरवं वंशमुद्वहन् ।\nप्रतिज्ञां वितथां कुर्यामिति राजन्पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with joined hands, I appeased my mother: 'Mother, born of Shantanu and carrying on the Kuru line, I could never make my vow false.'"}},{"n":33,"text":"विशेषतस्त्वदर्थं च धुरि मा मां नियोजय ।\nअहं प्रेष्यश्च दासश्च तवाम्ब सुतवत्सले ॥","meaning":{"en":"And especially for your sake, do not place me on the yoke. Mother, so fond of your son, I am your servant and slave."}},{"n":34,"text":"एवं तामनुनीयाहं मातरं जनमेव च ।\nअयाचं भ्रातृदारेषु तदा व्यासं महामुनिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus I soothed my mother and the people. Then I asked the great sage Vyasa for my brother's wives."}},{"n":35,"text":"सह मात्रा महाराज प्रसाद्य तमृषिं तदा ।\nअपत्यार्थमयाचं वै प्रसादं कृतवांश्च सः ।\nत्रीन्स पुत्रानजनयत्तदा भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Together with my mother I pleased that sage, great king, and asked for children. He granted the favor and begot three sons then, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":36,"text":"अन्धः करणहीनेति न वै राजा पिता तव ।\nराजा तु पाण्डुरभवन्महात्मा लोकविश्रुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your father, being blind and lacking a faculty, was not king; Pandu, the great-souled, famed in the world, became king."}},{"n":37,"text":"स राजा तस्य ते पुत्राः पितुर्दायाद्यहारिणः ।\nमा तात कलहं कार्षी राज्यस्यार्धं प्रदीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was king, and his sons are the heirs of their father's wealth. My son, do not make a quarrel; let half the kingdom be given."}},{"n":38,"text":"मयि जीवति राज्यं कः संप्रशासेत्पुमानिह ।\nमावमंस्था वचो मह्यं शममिच्छामि वः सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"While I live, who here could rule the kingdom? Do not slight my words; I always want peace for you."}},{"n":39,"text":"न विशेषोऽस्ति मे पुत्र त्वयि तेषु च पार्थिव ।\nमतमेतत्पितुस्तुभ्यं गान्धार्या विदुरस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"My son, I make no difference between you and them, King. This is also the opinion of your father, Gandhari and Vidura."}},{"n":40,"text":"श्रोतव्यं यदि वृद्धानां मातिशङ्कीर्वचो मम ।\nनाशयिष्यसि मा सर्वमात्मानं पृथिवीं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you are to heed your elders, do not doubt my words. Do not destroy everything, yourself and the earth.\""}}]}]}